# Legal pages for gmojsoski.com, served inline by Caddy.
#
# WHY NOT IN THE SITE BUILD: /srv/site is wiped by `rsync -av --delete` in
# scripts/update-portfolio.sh on every `make portfolio-update`. A file dropped
# there would vanish at the next portfolio deploy, taking the Google OAuth
# consent screen's privacy policy link down with it. Serving it from config
# keeps it independent of the portfolio_v2 build.
#
# WHY 05-: config.d/*.caddy is imported in glob (alphabetical) order and handle
# blocks are first-match-wins. This file must sort BEFORE 10-gmojsoski-home
# so /privacy is claimed here rather than falling through to that block's
# try_files and 404ing. Do not renumber it above 10 without moving this route.
#
# CONTACT ADDRESS: the @ is written as the entity &#64; on purpose. Cloudflare's
# Email Address Obfuscation rewrites plain mailto links into a
# /cdn-cgi/l/email-protection stub that only resolves once its injected script
# runs, and the CSP below blocks that script, so the address rendered blank.
# Entity-encoding slips past the obfuscator and needs no JavaScript.
#
# EDITING: the body below must contain NO curly braces. Caddy performs
# placeholder substitution on `respond` bodies, so a `{` in a <style> block
# would be parsed as a placeholder. That is why every rule here is an inline
# style attribute instead of a stylesheet.

@legal_privacy {
	host gmojsoski.com
	path /privacy /privacy/
}
handle @legal_privacy {
	header {
		Content-Type "text/html; charset=utf-8"
		Cache-Control "public, max-age=3600"
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'"
		-Server
	}
	respond `<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Privacy Policy</title>
</head>
<body style="max-width:44rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2rem 1.25rem;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;line-height:1.65;color:#1a1a1a;background:#fff">
<h1 style="font-size:1.75rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem">Privacy Policy</h1>
<p style="color:#666;margin-top:0">Applies to the scheduling service at cal.gmojsoski.com. Last updated 25 September 2026.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-top:2rem">Who operates this service</h2>
<p>This is a personal, self-hosted scheduling service run by Goce Mojsoski. It is not a commercial product and has no employees, investors or third-party operators.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-top:2rem">What the service does</h2>
<p>It lets people view available time slots and book a meeting. To show accurate availability it needs to read when the operator is already busy, and to confirm a booking it needs to create a calendar event.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-top:2rem">Information collected</h2>
<p>From people booking a meeting: the name, email address and any notes they type into the booking form, plus the date and time chosen. From the operator connecting a calendar: the information described in the next section.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-top:2rem">Google user data</h2>
<p>If you connect a Google account, the service requests these permissions and uses them only as described:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>See and download your calendars</strong> (calendar.readonly): used solely to read existing busy periods so that already-occupied times are not offered for booking.</li>
<li><strong>Edit events on your calendars</strong> (calendar.events): used solely to create, update and cancel the events generated by bookings made through this service.</li>
<li><strong>Basic profile information</strong> (userinfo.profile): used solely to label which account a connected calendar belongs to, so multiple connected accounts can be told apart.</li>
</ul>
<p>Access is granted only through Google's consent screen and can be withdrawn at any time. The service does not read message content, contacts, files or any Google data beyond the permissions listed above.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-top:2rem">Limited use</h2>
<p>Use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" style="color:#0645ad">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements. Google user data is never sold, never used for advertising, never used to train machine learning or AI models, and never transferred to third parties except as required to provide the scheduling feature itself.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-top:2rem">Where data is stored</h2>
<p>All data, including Google access tokens, is stored on a self-hosted server operated privately by the operator. Access tokens are held encrypted. Nothing is stored with an external analytics, advertising or data-broker service. Email notifications are delivered through Gmail's SMTP service, which necessarily sees the contents of those notification emails.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-top:2rem">Retention and deletion</h2>
<p>Booking records are kept for as long as the service runs, so that past and upcoming meetings remain visible. Google account data is retained only while the connection is active. Disconnecting the Google account removes its stored tokens.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-top:2rem">Revoking access</h2>
<p>You can revoke this application's access to your Google account at any time at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" style="color:#0645ad">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. Revoking access stops all future reading and writing of calendar data.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-top:2rem">Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy, or requests to delete data held about you, can be sent to grmojsoski&#64;gmail.com.</p>

<p style="margin-top:2.5rem"><a href="https://gmojsoski.com" style="color:#0645ad">Back to gmojsoski.com</a></p>
</body>
</html>` 200
}
